  "body": "Parent: [#6024](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/6024) (licensing gate for the external corpus). Research source: prior-art doc `~/workspace/scratch/atlas-ingestion-brief-2026-11-04/prior-art-research.md` (2026-11-04). Follow-up 33 (Cluster 6). Consumers: the GitHub extraction task #6023 and the trace store (#6027).\n\n## Finding (research, in substance)\n\nGitHub ToS §D.5's neighboring text: the D.4–D.8 licenses \"end when you remove Your Content, **unless other Users have forked it**.\" An external corpus is not a fork within the Service, so the fork exception doesn't cover Atlas — a defensible corpus **honors source deletions**: if a comment is deleted or a repo goes private, Atlas purges on next sync. This is both an ethical norm and a risk reducer.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Deletion detection per source class (API state diff on sync; tombstones for vanished items).\n- Purge semantics: text + vectors removed; a **tombstone stays in the trace log** so historical feedback/traces referencing the purged result remain interpretable (\"this result was purged on <date> under deletion propagation\") without retaining the content.\n- Our own repos: same machinery, policy-gated (Drew may keep his own deleted comments; third-party comments in our repos follow the external rule).\n\n## Done looks like\n\nA design: detection, purge, tombstone shape, and the policy switch per zone (sibling decision under #6024).\n\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=muse state=filed source=main-chat-2026-11-04-wave2 -->",
